Z||000007||rogergarrison||02-07-2001||07:01 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by DaRkLoRD:<BR><B>Valvoline, STP and Slick 50??<P>aren't those like.. major Nascar sponsors??<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>actually dark, I think all 3 have dropped out for the most part. STP is only an associate on Petty car, Valvoline left Martin, dont remember anyone with slick50. btw did you notice how Trickles Duralube car always seem to blow up(not good advertising). Most of the cars only use those decals for contingency money, not really use the products...I know because I raced years ago in NASCAR. As far as STP, no one can use it legally since its an illegal additive as are any others in NASCAR rules.<P><p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 02-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||ChadMan||02-07-2001||08:27 AM||||What hurts is when you see some race driver or crew chief you respect on there hawking a product that turns out to be a scam.  I forget which product it was (maybe ZMAX?) but I saw A.J. Foyt on one of those infomercials swearing he uses it in his IRL cars.<P>Between badmouthing CART, punching Arie Luyendyk and hawking $hitty products, A.J. has sure lost respect in my book.||||reg||1
Z||000009||rogergarrison||02-07-2001||09:48 AM||||I think that might have been 'Restore' chad. Replate your cylinder walls from a can.......ya.......rite.<P>I think the last stuff i did try was Slick 50. I tried it in my Lincoln TC even though I had no probs with it at all. Right away it started using oil about a qt in 300 miles. I drained and refilled without it and went way back up. I think maybe it makes cyl walls so slick that the rings dont scrub properly, they have to have a little friction to drag on the cylinder walls. I come up with that theory because I noticed how rotten wipers work with Rain X on windshield. Id use either the wipers OR the Rain X, not both. <p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 02-07-2001).]||||reg||1
